When WASM execution fails (e.g., `tecOUT_OF_GAS`), `re.error().cost` contains gas consumed but is discarded. The WASM engine comment explicitly states the caller must write this cost to tx metadata, but `gasUsed` and `vmReturnCode` are never set on this path.
Helpful? Add 👍 / 👎

<details>
<summary>💡 Fix Suggestion</summary>

**Suggestion:** On the WASM error path (lines 451-455), `re.error().cost` contains the gas consumed but is silently discarded. Per the `WasmTER` documentation, the caller should write this cost to tx metadata. Add a call to `ctx_.setGasUsed()` when `re.error().cost` has a value, mirroring the success path. Since `WasmTER` has no `result` field, `setVMReturnCode` is not applicable on this path.

Replace the error block with:
```cpp
        else
        {
            auto const& err = re.error();
            JLOG(j_.debug()) << "WASM Failure: " + transHuman(err.ter);
            if (err.cost.has_value())
            {
                auto const errCost = err.cost.value();
                if (errCost >= 0 && errCost <= std::numeric_limits<uint32_t>::max())
                    ctx_.setGasUsed(static_cast<uint32_t>(errCost));
            }
            return err.ter;
        }
```

