Attacker-controlled cacheIdx can overflow on decrement. Validate before decrementing:

```suggestion
    if (cacheIdx <= 0 || cacheIdx >= maxCache) return error;
    cacheIdx--;
```

Integer overflow: decrementing unchecked guest value before bounds check. Validate range first:

```suggestion:-0+6
std::expected<int32_t, HostFunctionError>
normalizeCacheIndex(int32_t cacheIdx) const
{
    if (cacheIdx <= 0 || cacheIdx > maxCache)
        return std::unexpected(HostFunctionError::SlotOutRange);
    --cacheIdx;
    if (!cache_[cacheIdx])
        return std::unexpected(HostFunctionError::EmptySlot);
    return cacheIdx;
}
```

Integer overflow: `--cacheIdx` overflows if cacheIdx is INT32_MIN, causing UB. Validate before decrement:

```suggestion
    if (cacheIdx == std::numeric_limits<int32_t>::min()) {
        return std::unexpected(HostFunctionError::CacheIndexOutOfRange);
    }
    --cacheIdx;
```

